0,Maraghei dialect - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maraghei_dialect,"February 27, 2026 - Maraghei (Tati: مراغی، مراقی) is a dialect of the Tati language, spoken in the Gilan Province, and upper Rudbar area (Rudbar-e Alamut). The Maraghei Tati is closely related to Talysh and Gozarkhani, and falls under the Central Tatic (spoken in the Qazvin Province) subgroup.",Maraghei,Indo-European
1,Abd al-Qadir al-Maraghi - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abd_al-Qadir_al-Maraghi,"Abd al-Qadir al-Maraghi ibn Ghaybi (Persian: عبدالقادر مراغی; d. 1435) was a music theorist, composer and performer of the Timurid Empire. [1][2] A renowned writer on music and musician, his theories had a profound influence on subsequent Persian, Arab, and Turkish music. [3][4]",Maraghei,Indo-European
2,List of Indo-European languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Indo-European_languages,"1 month ago - This is a list of languages in the Indo-European language family. It contains a large number of individual languages, together spoken by roughly half the world's population. The Indo-European languages include some 449 (SIL estimate, 2018 edition) languages spoken by about 3.5 billion people ...",Maraghei,Indo-European
3,Music of Romania - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Romania,"4 days ago - Romania is a multicultural music environment, which includes active ethnic music scenes. Traditional Romanian folk music remains popular, and certain folk musicians have come to national, or even international, fame. Folk music is the oldest form of Romanian music, characterised by great vitality; ...",Maraghei,Indo-European
4,Maraghei dialect — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/maraghei_dialect,"The Maraghei dialect, also referred to as Maraghei Tati, is an endangered variety of the Tati language spoken primarily in the Alamut Valley, Rudbar-e Alamut, and adjacent regions of northwestern Iran",Maraghei,Indo-European
